We check the analyst's report. They state: "The email campaign generated higher average revenue per converted order than the paid_search campaign among new customers...". They discuss measure: average revenue per converted order. They explicitly state they chose that measure, noting the question is not precise and they chose average revenue per converted order. They also compare to paid_search. They note non-random assignment and adjust for segment, and note raw comparison would be confounded. So they satisfy: they specify measure, compare to paid_search, note non-random assignment. So pass.

Thus JSON: {"pass": true, "reason": "The analyst explicitly stated the success metric (average revenue per converted order), the comparator (paid_search), and noted the non‑random assignment of channels."}
